<assessmentItem xmlns="http://www.imsglobal.org/xsd/imsqti_v2p1" xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xsi:schemaLocation="http://www.imsglobal.org/xsd/imsqti_v2p1 http://www.imsglobal.org/xsd/qti/qtiv2p1/imsqti_v2p1p1.xsd" identifier="VE_IP_49" title="Question 49" adaptive="false" timeDependent="false"><responseDeclaration identifier="RESPONSE" cardinality="single" baseType="identifier"><correctResponse><value>b</value></correctResponse></responseDeclaration><outcomeDeclaration identifier="SCORE" cardinality="single" baseType="float" normalMaximum="1" normalMinimum="0"><defaultValue><value>0</value></defaultValue></outcomeDeclaration><itemBody><div><p>Which red-black tree requirement is violated by the tree below?  </p><img src="VE_IP_49_image_1.png" width="350px" alt="Red-black tree with black root node 78. 78's left child is red 65 and right child is red 82. 65's left child is black 58 and right child is black 72. 58's left child is red 45. 82's right child is black 92." /></div><choiceInteraction responseIdentifier="RESPONSE" shuffle="false" maxChoices="1" minChoices="0"><simpleChoice identifier="a" showHide="show" fixed="true"><div><p> All child nodes should have the same number of leaf nodes</p></div></simpleChoice><simpleChoice identifier="b" showHide="show" fixed="true"><div><p> All paths from a node to any null leaf descendant node must have the same number of black nodes </p></div></simpleChoice><simpleChoice identifier="c" showHide="show" fixed="true"><div><p> Red nodes need to have an equal number of leaf nodes</p></div></simpleChoice><simpleChoice identifier="d" showHide="show" fixed="true"><div><p> The root node should always be a red node with black leaf nodes</p></div></simpleChoice></choiceInteraction></itemBody><responseProcessing template="http://www.imsglobal.org/question/qti_v2p1/rptemplates/match_correct" /></assessmentItem>